From 73d1892741840de282ec42e9bce6d907bf833384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:33:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Phase 0: one ticker, one name per system, and a share
 receipt that agrees with itself
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cleanup before any GEU ledger work, so nothing new reuses an identifier whose
semantics still mean something else. No behaviour changes except the two money
records named below.

THE AIRDROP WAS STILL WRITING A DEAD TICKER

server/scripts/coin-airdrop.mjs:217,237 wrote `currency: "GC"` onto a
Transaction row and a LedgerEntry row on every run — money records in a
currency the rest of the system stopped using at the GC -> GEU rename. The
balances those rows explain are counted as GEU.

The guard that should have caught it, tests/geu-one-currency.test.mjs,
enumerates the files it checks by hand and the script was not among them, so
it passed throughout. It also made scripts/migrate-gc-to-geu.mjs
non-idempotent in effect: relabel the old rows, then the next airdrop writes
new ones.

A constant correct in one file and wrong in another is not a typo, it is two
sources of truth. New server/lib/coinTicker.js is the single one; server.js
and the airdrop both require it. The guard now covers the script, and its
file list carries a note about why a hand-written list is only as good as the
hand.

TWO SYSTEMS, ONE STRING, NAMES ONE CHARACTER APART

server.js held `COIN_CURRENCY = 'GEU'` (live Gloobal Coin, backed 1:1 by
CoinReserve) and `GEU_CURRENCY = 'GEU'` (the superseded growth prototype,
which creates value, writes User.geuBalance and GeuSupply, and is 503-gated
precisely because of this collision). Both post to `ledgerentries` with a
`currency` field, so a route querying by that string cannot tell them apart.

The prototype's constant is now GEU_PROTOTYPE_CURRENCY, with the collision
and its consequence written down at both declarations. 27 references renamed;
no behaviour change. The live constant keeps its name — it is the live coin.

A CROSS-BORDER SHARE RECEIPT STORED THE WRONG CURRENCY

merchantShareFlow.js passed `amount: cashback, currency` to issueReceiptPair.
At that call site `cashback` is cashbackCredit — the PAYER's figure, in the
PAYER's currency — while `currency` is the payment's destination currency,
the PAYEE's. So an India -> US share stored the rupee figure labelled USD.

The share Transaction one level up already used `cashbackCurrency || currency`
and was right; the receipt beneath it was never updated. It is the exact
defect that file's own header describes sixty lines above — "a row that shows
one side's figure under the other side's symbol" — left unfixed one level
down. Same-currency payments make the two identical, which is why it survived:
merchant-share-flow.test.mjs is INR-only and cross-currency-transfer.test.mjs
sets both cashback rates to 0, so no existing test had both conditions at
once.

Nothing reads the Receipt collection today, so this was latent. A stored audit
record that is wrong by a factor of the exchange rate is still wrong.

New server/tests/share-receipt-currency.test.mjs is that intersection: one
cross-border payment to a payee who shares, asserting both the figure and the
label on all four receipts. It needs MONGO_URI and has not been run here.

ALSO

- backend/services/api/gloobalApi.js:953,986 hardcoded "GEU" as a fallback
  while line 1097 correctly used COIN_CURRENCY. The guard only greps for
  'GC', so a hardcoded 'GEU' passed — the same drift the rename was meant to
  end.
- GET /api/coin/supply rounded all three figures with no currency argument,
  so toMinorUnit fell back to 2 decimals. These are reserve-currency figures
  and 16 of the 142 currencies in the master have no minor unit; a JPY
  reserve was reporting hundredths of a yen, and `backed` compared three
  numbers each rounded to a precision their currency does not have.
- models/Settlement.js described `rate` as sourceCurrency -> destinationCurrency.
  It is the other direction. Every piece of arithmetic in the codebase agrees
  with the correct one and only the comment was reversed — the kind of thing
  somebody reads once, believes, and inverts a figure on.
- server/tests/merchant-share-flow.test.mjs:161 asserted
  `metadata.noBalanceMovement === true`, which the code has not written for
  some time and which creator-share-ledger.test.mjs:157 asserts is ABSENT.
  The two suites contradicted each other and this one was failing on main
  before any of today's work. Corrected to the flag the code actually writes.

NOT DONE HERE, DELIBERATELY

POST /api/assets/claim-interest credits balance from a growth formula with no
Transaction and no LedgerEntry. It is on the Phase 1 defect list, but fixing
it is a financial behaviour change, not cleanup — and in a GEU world it is
unbacked issuance, which is product decision 28.8 in the architecture design.
It stays as it is until that is answered.

TESTS

Browser suite 1218 pass / 0 fail. financial-principles 224 / 0. DB-free server
suites 59 / 0. The two tests that changed are listed above with reasons; one
was failing before this work and one followed the ticker to its new home.
Not run: the 29 DB-backed server suites, including the new one.

