tests/idempotent-duplicate-response.test.mjs is failing on main, and it is a
real defect rather than a stale assertion.

All three duplicate branches of POST /api/transactions/send — the idempotency
pre-check, the 15-second same-amount window, and the index-race recovery after
commit — returned only `transaction` and `shareTransaction`. None of the
top-level figures the original response carried: debitAmount, sourceAmount,
sourceCurrency, destinationAmount, destinationCurrency, senderCurrency,
fxRate, fxRateSource, amountBasis, cashback, cashbackCurrency, cashbackRate,
payeeReceives, newBalance.

A client that reads those off the response got them on the first call and
undefined on the retry. With no debitAmount and no senderCurrency, the only
amount left in the payload is the receiver-currency face value — which is
exactly the gap that lets the sender's side be taken for the receiver's. Same
family as F5: a lost response must be answered from the record, and an answer
missing half the record is not that.

storedPaymentFacts() reads them back off the stored row's own metadata.
Nothing is recomputed and no live rate is consulted, so a retry a day later
answers with the figures that governed the payment rather than today's.

newBalance is the one that cannot come from metadata, because it was never
written there. It is read off the sender's LAST ledger line for that
transaction — the recorded balance after the payment completed — rather than
from the account's balance now, which is a different fact and would drift the
moment anything else moved. A missing ledger line leaves it null, which reads
as "not recorded" rather than as a number.

The 15-second window branch answers 409 and carries the facts too: that
response names an existing payment, and a client showing it should show that
payment's figures rather than fall back to the request it just sent.

Browser suite 1218 pass / 0 fail. DB-free server suites 59 / 0. The suite that
proves this one needs MONGO_URI and has not been run here — it is the suite
that was already red.

